&lt;p&gt;A dialysis patient came to the ED short of breath. The X-ray looked like pulmonary edema — probably fluid overloaded. Fig 1 is the ECG on arrival. Potassium: 6.1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When the patient was handed over to me, it was right when the second cardiac enzymes and potassium were due to be followed up.&lt;/p&gt;
